      Understanding <strong>Singapore GST (Goods and Services Tax)</strong>—often referred to globally as <strong>Singapore VAT</strong> or <em>singapur gst / gst singapura</em>—is essential for consumers, business owners, and international investors. Administered strictly by the <a href="https://www.iras.gov.sg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline">Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore (IRAS)</a>, the current Singapore GST rate stands at <strong>9%</strong> in 2026.
    </p>

    <!-- Key Takeaways Card -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 dark:border-primary/30 dark:bg-primary/10">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
        <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-white font-bold text-sm">✓</span>
