            <td class="p-3">10%</td>
            <td class="p-3 font-medium">Comparable (+1%)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 7 FAQs -->
    <h2 id="faqs" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">7. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the current GST rate in Singapore for 2026?</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm">The standard Goods and Services Tax (GST) rate in Singapore is 9%. It applies to all taxable sales of goods and services as well as goods imported into Singapore.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">When did Singapore's GST increase to 9%?</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm">Singapore's GST rate was increased in two steps: from 7% to 8% on January 1, 2023, and from 8% to 9% on January 1, 2024. The 9% rate continues through 2026.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the difference between GST and VAT in Singapore?</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm">In Singapore, GST (Goods and Services Tax) is the official terminology for VAT (Value-Added Tax). Both describe a multi-stage tax levied on domestic consumption.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How do I pay GST online to IRAS?</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm">Log in to the IRAS myTax Portal using Corppass, submit your quarterly Form F5 return, and pay via GIRO, PayNow QR, or FAST bank transfer.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What supplies are zero-rated for GST in Singapore?</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm">Exported goods and international services (such as cross-border transport and services provided to overseas entities) are zero-rated (0% GST).</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Links / Suggested Content -->
